From 238957b1a86e0f3593cac3419892ad06eb88ca74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:54:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] Round 9: Rank from a dense fixed-size contender table

Replace the per-train weighted-priority, waiting-start and tail vectors
with one 128-entry table of interleaved records indexed by train & 127,
so the ranking pass has no bounds checks and reads one record per
contender. Waiting starts are stored as exact f64 integers, so the
f64 difference equals the former integer wait conversion. The
independent domain validation passed against this round's CLI.

Workload: lean domain (48 candidates, 110 trains), 11 samples.
Before median: 1.029 ms. After median: 0.902 ms. Speedup: 1.14x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
